.TH "DEDB LSARCHIVE" "1" "2026-01-01" "0.0.17" "dedb lsarchive Manual"
.SH NAME
dedb\-lsarchive \- List an archive.org user's favorites as `archive:<id>` targets.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dedb lsarchive
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List an archive.org user's favorites as `archive:<id>` targets.
.PP
The user comes from the `archive_user` setting, or a prompt.
MS-DOS items only, unless --all.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-favorites\fP
List the archive.org user's public favorites. (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fP NAME
archive.org screen name to list, overriding the configured [archive] archive_user.
.TP
\fB\-\-dos\fP / \-\-all
--dos (default): only MS-DOS items. --all: every favorite.
.TP
\fB\-1\fP
Just `archive:<id>` per line - no title column.
